## Interface: 120100
## Title: Shopping Converter
## Notes: Adds an Auction House tab that converts an Auctionator shopping list into a TradeSkillMaster-compatible search string.
## Author: Tharavol, Claude
## Version: @project-version@
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Inscription_ParchmentVar06
## Category-enUS: Auction House
## X-License: MIT
## SavedVariables: ShoppingConverterDB
## Dependencies: Auctionator
## OptionalDeps: CraftSim

## X-ReleaseNotes: Adds a Converter tab to the Blizzard Auction House frame that turns an Auctionator shopping list into a TradeSkillMaster-compatible search string, ready to paste into TSM. Pick a list from the dropdown and the string is generated and selected automatically; each entry becomes TSM's i:<itemID>/x<qty> syntax, joined with semicolons, and crafting-reagent quality is preserved so a rank 1 reagent does not silently become rank 3. Output too long for TSM's search box is split into parts you can page through and paste one at a time. When CraftSim is installed, item IDs are read straight out of its craft queue, which makes the common case instant; every resolved item ID is also cached across sessions, so repeat conversions of an evolving queue do not re-query the Auction House. The tab is added through the embedded LibAHTab library rather than a manual AH tab hack, avoiding taint. Auctionator is required - the addon reads shopping lists through its public API and will not load without it. CraftSim and TradeSkillMaster are both optional; Shopping Converter never calls into TSM, it only produces the text. /shopconv (alias /shoppingconverter) opens the settings panel; /shopconv convert <list> converts a list from anywhere, away from the Auction House; /shopconv help lists every command. Source, issues and release notes: https://github.com/Tharavol/ShoppingConverter

